## 2. Class Words

  Production requirement
    NORTHSTAR 1.1, or a user-facing fail-closed hole, or a lie
    a stranger meets when that stranger uses the pin.
    A production gap may become a this-cycle `[ ]` row.

  Residual
    ROADMAP 5.1 stay-residual facts.
    NORTHSTAR later: full SMT, AArch64, device GPU, SGX/TDX/SEV,
    HITL, vscode `ooda-lsp.js`, `import ".h"`, paused install,
    `qa/e2e/*.sh` and broken fixtures in the `qa_master.oo` header.
    Residual stays in 5.1. It is not this-cycle leftover work.

  Moonshot
    Every `[ ]` row in MOONSHOTS.oot. Keep those rows there.
    Do not copy a moonshot into ROADMAP section 5 as open work.

  Ignored
    ROADMAP 5.3 and 5.4, copied verbatim below.
    No new oodac row. No new org-std or product-std row.

